## Document map

This is the inverted index. Every `Topics` value must match a topic key in the
`Topic map`. Every document in the documentation tree must appear here or be
listed under `Index health`.

| Document | Type | Authority | Freshness | Topics | Read when | Skip when | Size | Keywords | Anchors |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `<path>` | guide | canonical | verified YYYY-MM-DD | <topic keys> | <Question types> | <When irrelevant> | S/M/L | <Terms> | `<path>` -> <section> |

Document types may include `overview`, `concept`, `procedure`, `runbook`,
`architecture`, `contract`, `reference`, `decision`, `history`, or `generated`.

Authority values:

- `instruction`: applicable project instructions such as `AGENTS.md`.
- `canonical`: preferred current source of truth.
- `supporting`: useful context but not the primary source.
- `reference`: background or external reference.
- `optional`: useful for history or depth, skipped by default.
- `stale`: retained for history; never use as current truth without warning.

Freshness values should identify when a source was last verified. Mark sources
as `stale`, `superseded`, `conflicted`, or `unavailable` when applicable.

